 abstract = {The changing technologies and internet are playing a significant role in tourism and hospitality business. The travellers as well as the tourism service providers use the social networking sites on regular bases, especially Online Travel Reviews (OTR). OTR are written by the travellers who share their experiences, give suggestions or express satisfaction/dissatisfaction after product consumption. The objectives of this study are- 1) to examine the relevance of social networking sites and OTR in tourism, 2) to discuss relationship between the OTR {\&} UGC and 3) to examine the present scenario of OTR in tourism business. Results indicate that reviews are helpful in potential travellers{\grq} decision makings especially at the planning phase. OTR are considered more effective to the potential tourists, in spite of the information given by travel service providers. Trustworthiness of OTR is the major problems faced by travellers. The hoteliers need to manage and respond to the reviews in an effective way. Consumers should be encouraged to post comments on the review sites. The tourism stockholders need to decide their e-commerce strategies for their betterment.},
